# tally 2.1.8 item 77 (#201), E §4.1 step 2 and L §4.4: a test of a window-dated movement that comes out one way on
# some of its days and another on the rest is the window's hole, as far as the refusal or the other class would reach.
# early is dated in window(2025-12-30, 2026-01-03) across the run's start, so it is left out on two days and booked on
# three: s1 is the hole and s2 splits it. late's window crosses the run's end, already its hole (e1). 2.1.7's refcore
# booked early (100.00 PLN). The plan's i77c.
# tally 2.2 (2.2-4): the clause `windows each` is cut; its asks are the plain line, the hole with each unknown day it
# carries named (`unknown day:`, 2.2-11). A caller who takes the window as one day pins its cell.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2025-12-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input ws: date
input we: date

move early: transfers
  on ws
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

move late: transfers
  on we
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-11-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  ws = window(2025-12-30, 2026-01-03) "s"
  we = window(2026-06-28, 2026-07-03) "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask s1: bal(konto, 2026-01-31)
ask s2: bal(konto, 2026-01-31)
ask s3: flows(early, 2026-01)
ask s4: count(t in transfers over 2025-12-01 .. 2026-01-31)
ask e1: bal(konto, 2026-06-30)
ask e2: bal(konto, 2026-06-30)
=== expect
e1: ?"date within window(2025-12-30, 2026-01-03) not precise enough for a balance" (early) ?"date within window(2026-06-28, 2026-07-03) not precise enough for a balance" (late)
  unknown day: we
  unknown day: ws
  cut 2025-12-01
e2: ?"date within window(2025-12-30, 2026-01-03) not precise enough for a balance" (early) ?"date within window(2026-06-28, 2026-07-03) not precise enough for a balance" (late)
  unknown day: we
  unknown day: ws
  cut 2025-12-01
s1: ?"date within window(2025-12-30, 2026-01-03) not precise enough for a balance" (early)
  unknown day: ws
  cut 2025-12-01
s2: ?"date within window(2025-12-30, 2026-01-03) not precise enough for a balance" (early)
  unknown day: ws
  cut 2025-12-01
s3: ?"date within window(2025-12-30, 2026-01-03) not precise enough for flows of early" (early)
  unknown day: ws
  cut 2025-12-01
s4: 1
  cut 2025-12-01
